@startuml end-to-end-telemetry
!theme plain
title Dynamic View — End-to-End Telemetry Pipeline (Full System Flow)
autonumber

' === Skin Parameters ===
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam maxMessageSize 200
skinparam sequenceParticipantPadding 20
skinparam sequenceBoxPadding 10

' === Participants ===
actor "System\nAdministrator" as Admin
participant "Management UI\n(MUI)" as MUI
participant "CnSS REST API\n(FastAPI)" as REST
participant "Traffic Processor\n(TP)" as TP
participant "Communication\nNode (CN)" as CN
participant "CnSS Ingestion\nWorker" as Ingest
participant "Background\nFlusher" as Flusher
participant "Redis\n(Ephemeral)" as Redis
database "TimescaleDB\n(Persistent)" as DB
participant "CnSS Reporting\nWorker (1Hz)" as Report
participant "CnSS WebSocket\nService" as WS

== Phase 1: Authentication & Channel Discovery (REST) ==

Admin -> MUI : Login with credentials
MUI -> REST : POST /api/v1/auth/login\n{username, password}
REST -> REST : Validate via Argon2id hash
REST --> MUI : 200 OK { access_token (JWT),\nrole, scope[] }

MUI -> REST : GET /api/v1/channels\nAuthorization: Bearer <JWT>
REST -> Redis : SISMEMBER jwt:revoked <jti>
Redis --> REST : 0 (not revoked)
REST -> DB : SELECT channels\n(filtered by scope)
DB --> REST : Channel list
REST --> MUI : 200 OK { channels: [\n{channel_id, is_active, last_activity}\n] }

Admin -> MUI : Select channel\n"bridge-berlin-01"

== Phase 2: WebSocket Connection & Initial Subscription ==

MUI -> WS : WSS connect\n/api/v1/ws/telemetry?\ntoken=<JWT>&channel_id=bridge-berlin-01
WS -> Redis : SISMEMBER jwt:revoked <jti>
Redis --> WS : 0 (valid)
WS -> WS : Verify channel in JWT scope
WS --> MUI : 101 Switching Protocols

MUI -> WS : {"action": "subscribe",\n"target": "telemetry",\n"channel_id": "bridge-berlin-01"}
WS -> WS : Compute query_hash =\nSHA256(channel_id + target + params)
WS -> Redis : SET sub:registry:{hash}\nSADD sub:listeners:{hash} client_id\nSADD sub:active_hashes {hash}

note over WS, DB
  **RACE-CONDITION SAFE ORDERING:**
  1. SUBSCRIBE to Redis Pub/Sub FIRST
  2. THEN query TimescaleDB for snapshot
  3. THEN push snapshot to client
  Prevents missing updates that arrive
  between DB query and Pub/Sub subscription.
end note

WS -> Redis : SUBSCRIBE ws:push:{hash}
WS -> DB : SELECT aggregated metrics\nfrom telemetry_1s\n(Continuous Aggregate)
DB --> WS : Initial snapshot data
WS --> MUI : telemetry_update\n(Initial Snapshot)

== Phase 3: Physical Data Plane (Wire-Speed Forwarding) ==

note over TP
  TP's Data Plane operates independently
  as a transparent inline bridge on FPGA.
  Failure in monitoring NEVER impacts
  core packet forwarding (US-005, US-009).
end note

loop Continuous Network Traffic
    TP -> TP : Receive packets from\nSNIFF_INTERFACE_IN
    TP -> TP : Forward at wire speed\nto SNIFF_INTERFACE_OUT
    TP -> TP : Extract metadata\n(src_ip, dst_ip, ports, direction)
    TP -> CN : Raw packet metadata\n(Local UDP/IPC)
end

== Phase 4: Telemetry Batching (Communication Node) ==

note over CN
  CN batches packets into fixed time windows
  (e.g., window_ms: 50) and enforces UDP MTU
  constraint (< 1400 bytes) to prevent
  IP fragmentation and silent UDP drops.
end note

loop Every window_ms (e.g., 50ms)
    CN -> CN : Aggregate buffered packets\ninto TelemetryBatch
    CN -> CN : Increment 64-bit\nsequence counter
    CN -> Ingest : UDP TelemetryBatch JSON\n{channel_id, sequence,\nwindow_ms, packets[]}
end

== Phase 5: High-Performance Ingestion & Redis Buffering ==

Ingest -> Redis : HGET channel:seq:{channel_id}
Redis --> Ingest : last_sequence

alt incoming_sequence > last_sequence + 1
    Ingest -> Ingest : Calculate dropped_batches\n= incoming - last - 1
    Ingest -> Redis : HINCRBY channel:state:{channel_id}\ndropped_delta <dropped_count>
else incoming_sequence <= last_sequence
    Ingest -> Ingest : Ignore out-of-order\n(graceful handling)
else last_sequence - incoming > 1,000,000
    Ingest -> Ingest : CN reboot detected!\nForce-update baseline
end

Ingest -> Redis : HSET channel:seq:{channel_id}\nlast_sequence = incoming
Ingest -> Redis : LPUSH udp:buffer:{channel_id}\n<raw packet metadata>
Ingest -> Redis : LTRIM udp:buffer:{channel_id}\n0 99999 (cap at 100k, prevent OOM)
Ingest -> Redis : HSET channel:state:{channel_id}\nlast_activity_at = NOW()\n(EXPIRE 6s)

== Phase 6: Background Flush to TimescaleDB ==

loop Periodic Background Flush
    Flusher -> Redis : Lua script: atomic LPOP\nN items from udp:buffer
    Redis --> Flusher : Batch of raw packets
    Flusher -> DB : Batch INSERT INTO packet_flows\n(time, channel_id, direction,\nsrc_ip, dst_ip, src_port, dst_port)
    DB --> Flusher : Commit OK
end

note over DB
  TimescaleDB hypertable auto-partitions
  by time. Retention policy: 7 days.
  Continuous aggregate telemetry_1s
  pre-computes 1-second buckets.
end note

== Phase 7: 1Hz Reporting Worker (Aggregation Loop) ==

loop Every 1 second
    Report -> Redis : SMEMBERS sub:active_hashes
    Redis --> Report : {hash1, hash2, ...}
    
    Report -> Redis : SCARD sub:listeners:{hash}
    Redis --> Report : N listeners
    
    alt N > 0 (subscribers exist)
        Report -> Redis : GET sub:registry:{hash}
        Redis --> Report : {target, params, channel_id}
        Report -> Report : Build parameterized SQL\n(whitelist sort_by/sort_order)
        Report -> DB : SELECT time_bucket(...),\nSUM(direction=0), SUM(direction=1)\nFROM telemetry_1s
        DB --> Report : Aggregated metrics
        Report -> Redis : PUBLISH ws:push:{hash}\n{type: "telemetry_update",\nmetrics, dropped_batches}
    else N == 0
        Report -> Report : Skip SQL query\n(save DB resources)
    end
    
    Report -> Redis : Lua: atomic read/reset\ndropped_delta per channel
    Report -> DB : UPDATE channels\nSET is_active = TRUE,\ndropped += delta,\nlast_activity_at = NOW()\nWHERE activity detected
    DB --> Report : Updated rows
end

== Phase 8: Real-Time Push to MUI ==

Redis -> WS : Pub/Sub message on\nws:push:{hash}
WS -> WS : Lookup listeners for hash\nfrom sub:listeners:{hash}
WS -> WS : Inject client-specific "id"\ninto payload
WS -> MUI : WS Push: telemetry_update\n{channel_id, is_active: true,\nmetrics: {direction_in, direction_out},\ndropped_batches, timestamp}

MUI -> MUI : Reactively update\nbinary activity indicator\n+ bidirectional packet graphs

== Phase 9: Channel Timeout Detection ==

note over Report
  If CN stops sending telemetry
  (network issue, CN crash, etc.),
  Reporting Worker detects timeout.
end note

loop Every 1 second (timeout check)
    Report -> DB : UPDATE channels\nSET is_active = FALSE\nWHERE last_activity_at <\nNOW() - INTERVAL '5 seconds'
    DB --> Report : List of timed-out\nchannel_ids
    
    loop For each timed-out channel
        Report -> Redis : SMEMBERS channel:subs:{channel_id}
        Redis --> Report : Affected query_hashes
        
        loop For each affected hash
            Report -> Redis : PUBLISH ws:push:{hash}\n{is_active: false}
            Redis -> WS : Pub/Sub message
            WS -> MUI : WS Push: telemetry_update\n{is_active: false}
            MUI -> MUI : Switch indicator to RED\n(stop graph updates)
        end
    end
end

note over MUI
  **CLIENT-SIDE FALLBACK:**
  If MUI receives no telemetry_update
  within 6000ms, it locally assumes
  is_active = false (defensive design).
end note

== Phase 10: Session Heartbeat & Cleanup ==

loop Every 5 seconds (heartbeat)
    WS -> Redis : EXPIRE ws:session:{client_id} 10s
    Redis --> WS : OK
end

note over WS, Redis
  If WebSocket Service crashes:
  - Session keys auto-expire (TTL 10s)
  - Ghost Cleaner removes stale listeners
  - Clients reconnect and re-subscribe
  
  If Redis restarts (no persistence):
  - Buffers & sequence baselines lost
  - System gracefully resets and resumes
  - Accepted trade-off for max IOPS
end note

@enduml